            <ArticleTitle>[Longterm therapy of angina pectoris patients with a new beta-receptor blocker (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1123-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The beta-receptor blocker Timolol was investigated for 28 weeks in a double blind trial and then for up to 100 weeks in an open trial in patients with angina pectoris. In both phases of the investigation. Timolol caused a quite marked regression in the frequency of attacks and in the pulse rate at rest. The evaluation of therapeutic success by doctor and patient was positive for Timolol.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
